{"id":"ordinarium.credo","title":"Credo","category":"ordinarium","section":"missa-catechumenorum","variant":"missae","sung":true,"st":"working-edition","ad":5,"adw":2,"about":{"pl":"Symbol nicejsko-konstantynopolitański, odmawiany po Ewangelii w każdą niedzielę i w większe święta, a opuszczany we Mszach za zmarłych. Na słowa Et incarnátus est, w których Symbol wyznaje Słowo, które stało się ciałem, wszyscy przyklękają. Jego artykuły idą od Ojca i Syna do Ducha Świętego, Kościoła, jednego chrztu, wskrzeszenia umarłych i życia wiecznego.","en":"The Nicene-Constantinopolitan Creed, said after the Gospel on every Sunday and on the greater feasts, and left out in Masses for the Dead. All genuflect at Et incarnátus est, where the Creed confesses the Word made flesh. Its articles run from the Father and the Son to the Holy Spirit, the Church, one baptism, the resurrection of the dead and the life of the world to come."},"ac":{"pl":[112,113],"en":[112,113]},"seg":[{"id":"s01","type":"rubric","text":"Deinde ad medium Altaris extendens, elevans et iungens manus, dicit, si dicendum est, Credo in unum Deum, et prosequitur iunctis manibus.","an":8,"nr":{"pl":"Na środku ołtarza kapłan wyciąga i unosi ręce, składa je, odmawia Credo, jeśli jest przewidziane, i kontynuuje ze złożonymi rękami. Pochyla głowę ku krzyżowi przy in unum Deum, przy Iesum Christum i przy simul adorátur, a przy Et vitam ventúri sǽculi żegna się od czoła do piersi.","en":"At the middle of the altar, the priest extends and raises his hands, joins them, says the Creed if prescribed, and continues with hands joined. The priest bows his head to the cross at in unum Deum, at Iesum Christum and at simul adorátur, and signs himself from forehead to breast at Et vitam ventúri sǽculi."}},{"id":"s02","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","participation":{"lecta":{"gradus":3,"source":"DMS 31 c"},"cantu":{"gradus":2,"source":"DMS 25 b"}},"w":[{"i":"w001","f":"Credo","l":"credo","m":232},{"i":"w002","f":"in","l":"in","m":3,"h":"w004"},{"i":"w003","f":"unum","l":"unus","m":96,"h":"w004"},{"i":"w004","f":"Deum","l":"deus","p":",","m":35},{"i":"w005","f":"Patrem","l":"pater","m":162},{"i":"w006","f":"omnipoténtem","l":"omnipotens","p":",","m":96,"h":"w005"},{"i":"w007","f":"factórem","l":"factor","m":162},{"i":"w008","f":"cæli","l":"caelum","m":68},{"i":"w009","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w010","f":"terræ","l":"terra","p":",","m":64},{"i":"w011","f":"visibílium","l":"visibilis","m":114,"h":"w012"},{"i":"w012","f":"ómnium","l":"omnis","m":114,"s":true},{"i":"w013","f":"et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w014","f":"invisibílium","l":"invisibilis","p":".","m":114,"h":"w012"}],"tr":{"pl":"Wierzę w jednego Boga, Ojca wszechmogącego, Stworzyciela nieba i ziemi, wszystkich rzeczy widzialnych i niewidzialnych.","en":"I believe in one God, the almighty Father, maker of heaven and earth, of all things visible and invisible."},"tc":{"pl":[110],"en":[111]},"g":{"pl":["wierzę","w","jednego","Boga","Ojca","wszechmogącego","twórcę","nieba","i","ziemi","widzialnych","wszystkich","i","niewidzialnych"],"en":["I believe","in","one","God","the Father","almighty","maker","of heaven","and","of earth","visible","of all things","and","invisible"]},"fn":{"pl":{"w001":"Łączy się z „in” (w002) i biernikiem."},"en":{"w001":"Takes “in” (w002) with the accusative."}}},{"id":"s03","type":"verse","speaker":"sacerdos","voice":"clara","participation":{"lecta":{"gradus":3,"source":"DMS 31 c"},"cantu":{"gradus":2,"source":"DMS 25 b"}},"w":[{"i":"w015","f":"Et","l":"et","m":15},{"i":"w016","f":"in","l":"in","m":3,"h":"w018"},{"i":"w017","f":"unum","l":"unus","m":96,"h":"w018"},{"i":"w018","f":"Dóminum","l":"dominus","m":35},{"i":"w019","f":"Iesum","l":"Iesus","m":38},{"i":"w020","f":"Christum","l":"Christus","p":",","m":35},{"i":"w021","f":"Fílium","l":"filius","m":35},{"i":"w022","f":"Dei","l":"deus","m":54},{"i":"w023","f":"unigénitum","l":"unigenitus","p":".","m":96,"h":"w021"}],"tr":{"pl":"I w jednego Pana, J